# Cloudflare Pages routing (S13.1, S13.17).
#
# Every marketing route is prerendered to its own static file (S15.1) and the docs build is mounted
# at /docs, so Cloudflare serves those static files directly. There is deliberately NO catch-all SPA
# fallback: an unmatched path falls through to the branded 404.html (dist/404.html, written by
# gen-seo.mjs) with a real 404 status, instead of masking bad URLs behind a 200 homepage.

# --- Host canonicalization (301) ------------------------------------------------------------------
# One hostname must own every URL, or the same page accrues links and crawl budget under two.
# Cloudflare Pages already normalizes a trailing slash (308 /x/ -> /x) and enforces HTTPS on custom
# domains, so those two need no rule here — but nothing collapses www onto the apex by default, and
# the canonical tags all point at https://mcpfold.com.
https://www.mcpfold.com/*   https://mcpfold.com/:splat   301!

# --- Legacy / renamed path redirects (301) -------------------------------------------------------
/home             /                  301
/index.html       /                  301
/servers          /directory         301
/server/*         /directory/:splat  301
/download         /install           301
/docs.html        /docs              301
